{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_015aNYS3ddUoxHR5grYiHTrw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed this run:\n\n**Written:** `ai-engineering/answers/07-013-latencycostrelevancy-tradeoff-triangle.md`\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Framing:** Probes whether you can reason about all three axes simultaneously, not optimize one greedily\n- **Answer:** Three-axis framework (latency=p95, cost=$/query, relevancy=RAGAS Recall@5) with five concrete tension examples showing how each decision moves all three levers\n- **The win-win insight:** Cross-encoder reranking on top-20→3 simultaneously improves relevancy (+16% Recall@5), cuts latency (−26%), and reduces cost (−57%) by shortening the context passed to the LLM — the rare case where you don't have to trade off\n- **Concrete table:** Baseline GPT-4o system at $0.0105/query, 4.2s p95 → $0.0013/query, 1.4s after hybrid retrieval + rerank + model tiering + semantic cache\n- **Pitfalls:** Treating top-k as pure relevancy knob (ignores latency/cost), treating semantic caching as a free win (threshold tradeoff), conflating batching (throughput) with latency optimization\n\n**Remaining in Next:** Q14, Q15, Q16, then validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":77134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0a637f4-e9d9-46c7-9d47-04ee8467f73b","uuid":"92d482ca-1d4e-4523-8004-3d4e30610577"}
